  "findings": [
    "The confirmatory sentence-split candidates were rejected before detector scanning on both holdout samples: they kept the coarse C2 label but lowered reading grade outside the explicit source-relative envelope.",
    "Both AI baselines were saturated at 100% in three repeats on ZeroGPT and Scribbr.",
    "All four preregistered quality-passing comparators remained 100% in both primary services in screening scans.",
    "The p04 human control scored 42.9% in ZeroGPT and 0% in Scribbr; Sapling assigned 96.4% and 100% to the two human controls.",
    "Copyleaks accepted an exact SHA-bound input but never reached a terminal result, so no score was recorded.",
    "The calibration sentence-split effect did not pass the preregistered holdout quality contract and is not transferable as a Palimpsest rule."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Only two scientific holdout samples were tested; failure here rejects the current rule but does not characterize every possible local sentence split.",
    "Both AI baselines were at the displayed ceiling, so primary services could not resolve small adverse or beneficial changes in comparator scores.",
    "H1 was not sent to detector services because preregistration required rejection after a failed quality screen.",
    "Sapling was diagnostic only because its human controls produced severe false positives.",
    "Copyleaks did not reach a terminal state and is excluded from score comparisons.",
    "No screenshots were retained; scored observations are DOM-only with post-terminal full-text SHA binding.",
    "The source-as-reference style metric is low-reliability on 97–132 word texts."
  ]
